.TH "tabtomd" "1" "v1.0.2" "Version v1.0.2" "General Commands Manual"
.SH NAME
\f[B]tabtomd\f[R] \- Convert tab delimited data to Markdown table
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\f[B]tabtomd\f[R] [\f[B]COMMAND\f[R]] [\f[B]OPTIONS\f[R]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\f[CR]tabtomd\f[R] is a versatile command\-line utility for converting
tab\-delimited text into Markdown table format.
It supports input from either the system clipboard or a specified file
and allows the output to be written to standard output or saved to a
file.
.PP
The tool includes an optional \f[CR]\-\-pretty\f[R] flag to align
vertical bars in the Markdown table, improving readability and
presentation.
It is especially useful for generating Markdown tables for
documentation, reports, or other structured data presentations.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\f[B]completion\f[R]
Generate an autocompletion script for the specified shell.
.TP
\f[B]file\f[R]
Convert a tab\-delimited file to a Markdown table.
.TP
\f[B]help\f[R]
Display help information for any command.
.TP
\f[B]paste\f[R]
Convert tab\-delimited data from the system clipboard.
.TP
\f[B]version\f[R]
Display the \f[CR]tabtomd\f[R] version and build information.
.SH FLAGS
.TP
\f[B]\-\-output \f[BI]string\f[B]\f[R]
Specify a file to save the generated Markdown table.
.TP
\f[B]\-\-pretty\f[R]
Align vertical bars in the Markdown table for better readability.
.TP
\f[B]\-\-print\f[R]
Print the Markdown table to standard output.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Convert a tab\-delimited file to a Markdown table and print it to the screen
\f[CR]tabtomd file tsv_file.txt \-\-print\f[R]
.SS Convert a tab\-delimited file to an aligned Markdown table and print it to the screen
\f[CR]tabtomd file tsv_file.txt \-\-pretty \-\-print\f[R]
.SS Convert a tab\-delimited file to an aligned Markdown table and save it to a file
\f[CR]tabtomd file tsv_file.txt \-\-output markdown_table.md \-\-pretty\f[R]
.SS Convert tab\-delimited text from the clipboard to a Markdown table and print it to the screen
\f[CR]tabtomd paste \-\-print\f[R]
.SS Convert tab\-delimited text from the clipboard to an aligned Markdown table and print it to the screen
\f[CR]tabtomd paste \-\-pretty \-\-print\f[R]
.SS Convert tab\-delimited text from the clipboard to an aligned Markdown table and save it to a file
\f[CR]tabtomd paste \-\-output markdown_table.md \-\-pretty\f[R]
.SS Display help for the \f[CR]file\f[R] command
\f[CR]tabtomd file \-\-help\f[R] \f[B]OR\f[R]
\f[CR]tabtomd help file\f[R]
